# Gym Management System - Quick Start Guide

## Prerequisites
✅ MySQL 8.0.46 - Installed and Running (Service: MySQL80)
✅ Java 21 - Configured in build.gradle
✅ Gradle - Wrapper included

## Database Setup

### 1. Set MySQL Password (PowerShell)
```powershell
# Set for current session
$env:MYSQL_PASSWORD = "your_mysql_root_password"

# Or set permanently (Windows)
[System.Environment]::SetEnvironmentVariable('MYSQL_PASSWORD', 'your_password', 'User')
```

### 2. Verify Database Connection (Optional)
```powershell
# Connect to MySQL to verify
& "C:\Program Files\MySQL\MySQL Server 8.0\bin\mysql.exe" -u root -p

# In MySQL shell, verify/create database:
SHOW DATABASES;
CREATE DATABASE IF NOT EXISTS gymapp;
USE gymapp;
```

The application will automatically create the database if it doesn't exist due to:
```
createDatabaseIfNotExist=true
```

## Running the Application

### Start the server:
```powershell
cd "c:\Users\user\Desktop\gymapp (1)\gymapp"
.\gradlew.bat bootRun
```

### Expected Output:
```
Started GymappApplication in X.XXX seconds
Tomcat started on port 8080
```

## Accessing the API

### Swagger UI (Interactive Documentation)
```
http://localhost:8080/swagger-ui.html
```

### OpenAPI JSON Specification
```
http://localhost:8080/api-docs
```

### Direct API Endpoints
```
GET    http://localhost:8080/api/gym-classes
POST   http://localhost:8080/api/gym-classes
GET    http://localhost:8080/api/gym-classes/{uuid}
PUT    http://localhost:8080/api/gym-classes/{uuid}
DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/gym-classes/{uuid}
GET    http://localhost:8080/api/gym-classes?trainerId=1
```

## Testing with Swagger UI

1. Open http://localhost:8080/swagger-ui.html
2. Click on "Gym Classes" to expand
3. Click "Try it out" on any endpoint
4. Fill in the request body (for POST/PUT)
5. Click "Execute" to test

### Example POST Request Body:
```json
{
  "name": "Morning Yoga",
  "trainerId": 1,
  "capacity": 20,
  "dateTime": "2026-07-28T10:00:00"
}
```

**Note:** You'll need to create a Trainer first before creating GymClasses. We can add seed data or create other entities next.

## Troubleshooting

### Port 8080 already in use:
```properties
# Add to application.properties
server.port=8081
```

### MySQL Connection Failed:
- Verify MySQL80 service is running: `Get-Service MySQL80`
- Check credentials in application.properties
- Ensure MYSQL_PASSWORD environment variable is set

### Database Not Created:
```sql
-- Connect to MySQL and run:
CREATE DATABASE gymapp CHARACTER SET utf8mb4 COLLATE utf8mb4_unicode_ci;
```

